+# R39 Type-Check Plane — Evaluation Verdict (2026-10-28)
+
+Lane: **R39** (number from `docs/SCOUT_RADAR_INDEX.md` allocation rule, printed "next free: R39" after drift pass 3)
+Source: **#2029** (ecosystem-scout Job 478520; verdict requested: `evaluate`)
+Scope of this evaluation: adopt the scout's three adopt-grade annotation corrections, expand them by exact-class adjacency, and rule on the strict mypy gate proposal.
+
+## Verdict
+
+| Proposal element | Verdict | Basis |
+|---|---|---|
+| Annotation-correctness fixes (adopt-grade class) | **ADOPT — landed in this PR** | 6 sites across 4 files; each eliminated a live `mypy 2.4.0` error, zero new errors introduced (before/after receipts below) |
+| Strict mypy gate wired into CI now | **DEFER** | Sampled precision ~23% (3 real / 13 independent findings); 246-error mountain concentrated in documentable FP classes; wiring a gate at this precision would manufacture red CI without trust gains |
+| Future gate preconditions | **REGISTERED (this doc)** | Three hard preconditions listed below; gate re-proposal after they hold |
+
+## Adopted fixes (the annotation-lies class)
+
+Every site below was verified against actual usage before editing; the runtime contract was already the wider one — only the annotation lied.
+
+| File:line (HEAD `fc3c1a0`) | Was | Now | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `scripts/ci/vendored_tree_guard.py:131` | `by_top: Mapping[str, list[AddedFile]] = {}` | `dict[str, list[AddedFile]]` | `.setdefault()` mutates (line 132); `Mapping` is the read-only protocol; mypy `attr-defined` error confirmed at HEAD |
+| `scripts/ci/vendored_tree_guard.py:34` | `from collections.abc import Mapping, Sequence` | `from collections.abc import Sequence` | `Mapping` left unused after the fix above (rg: zero remaining references) |
+| `scripts/ci/staggered_rolling_train.py:197` | `commit_files: Mapping[str,] \| None` | `Mapping[str, tuple[str, ...]] \| None` | `Mapping[str,]` = 1 type arg (mypy `type-arg` at HEAD); values are path tuples at every call/definition site (`staggered_rolling_train.py:329`, `three_way_check` `.get(cur, ())`) |
+| `scripts/ci/hourly_satellite_batcher.py:261` | `commit_files: Mapping[str,]` | `Mapping[str, tuple[str, ...]]` | Same malformed syntax in the callee of the site above — exact-class adjacency, same value contract |
+| `scripts/ci/hourly_satellite_batcher.py:316` | `commit_files: Mapping[str,] \| None` | `Mapping[str, tuple[str, ...]] \| None` | Same class, `plan_batches` signature; repo-wide rg found exactly these 3 `Mapping[str,]` sites, all fixed |
+| `scripts/ci/bridge_opener_hardening_reference.py:43` | `wo_body: str` | `wo_body: str \| None` | In-file self-test line 187 asserts `extract_evidence_sections(None) == ""`; body guard `wo_body or ""` (line 52) already implemented the None-safe contract |
+| `scripts/ci/bridge_opener_hardening_reference.py:35` | `wo_body: str` | `wo_body: str \| None` | Docstring (line 38) already promises "empty/None body -> False (fail-closed, unchanged)"; annotation now matches the documented contract |
+
+Scope note: the scout's adopt-grade list named 3 files / 3 sites. This PR lands 6 sites in 4 files: the 3 additions are (a) the second `Mapping[str,]` site in `plan_batches` found by repo-wide rg of the identical syntax, (b) the callee `three_way_check` signature the caller feeds, (c) `has_reflection_evidence`, whose in-file docstring documents the None contract its annotation contradicted. No behavior changes anywhere — annotations and one import line only.
+
+## mypy 2.4.0 before/after (pinned, compiled wheel; profile `--explicit-package-bases --ignore-missing-imports`)
+
+Files under check: exactly the 4 touched files.
+
+- **Before (HEAD versions)**: 11 errors — includes the 5 target defects: `vendored_tree_guard.py:131 attr-defined` (Mapping.setdefault), `hourly_satellite_batcher.py:261 type-arg`, `hourly_satellite_batcher.py:316 type-arg`, `staggered_rolling_train.py:197 type-arg`, `bridge_opener_hardening_reference.py:187 arg-type` (None vs `str`).
+- **After (this PR)**: 6 errors — **all 5 target defects eliminated; 0 new errors**.
+- Remaining 6 are the scout's already-classified FP/pre-existing classes, out of adopt-grade scope by design:
+  - `staggered_rolling_train.py:291/293` — first-binding-wins rebinding FP (repro'd in scout's `audit/mypy_repro/`; runtime dispatches to the second def)
+  - `staggered_rolling_train.py:314` — intentional negative self-test (`active_slot("now")` inside expect-error block)
+  - `bridge_opener_hardening_reference.py:160/200`, `hourly_satellite_batcher.py:454` — pre-existing, unclaimed remainder (sampled-precision caveat unchanged)
+
+## Runtime verification receipts
+
+1. `py_compile` all 4 files — PASS (exit 0).
+2. In-file self-tests, all PASS after the fix:
+   - `bridge_opener_hardening_reference.py --self-test` → "self-test OK" (covers `extract_evidence_sections(None) == ""`)
+   - `hourly_satellite_batcher.py --self-test` → "self-test OK — hourly_satellite_batcher (issue #514 Tier 2 & Tier 3)"
+   - `staggered_rolling_train.py --self-test` → "self-test OK — staggered_rolling_train (issue #514 Tier 4)"
+   - `vendored_tree_guard.py --self-test` → "SELF-TEST OK: vendored_tree_guard"
+3. Residue scan: `rg 'Mapping\[str,\]'` over `scripts/ci/` → 0 hits; `rg Mapping` in `vendored_tree_guard.py` → 0 hits (import correct).
+4. Repo-wide syntax-class scan: `Mapping[str,]` count on main = 3 (this PR fixes all 3).
+
+## Gate preconditions (registered for the future gate re-proposal)
+
+1. **Pin the checker version** — gate must run a version-pinned mypy (today: 2.4.0) so error-code semantics are stable across the fleet's runners.
+2. **Regenerate `type: ignore` taxonomy under 2.x semantics** — the fleet's 171 `type: ignore` comments were written against 1.x codes; 2.x already drifts (`union-attr` not covered by `ignore[attr-defined]`). Until regenerated, a gate re-checks known sites.
+3. **Whitelist the designed negative self-tests** — at minimum `staggered_rolling_train.py:314`, `self_healing_reporter.py:196`, `bridge_opener_hardening_reference.py:187`; a gate that fails on fail-closed proofs is a false alarm machine.
+
+Re-proposal path: after preconditions 1–2 land, a shrink-only gate (per-file or per-class denylist that only shrinks) becomes evaluable; precision sampling should then be re-run on the regenerated-ignore state, not today's.
+
+## Benchmark honesty
+
+One dated mypy sweep (2.4.0, default semantics, 4-file scope) executed this cycle, before/after pairs archived in the PR evidence. No checker-vs-checker comparison, no runtime-behavior claims beyond the in-file self-tests. FP classifications beyond the 5 target defects are quoted from #2029's hand-verified taxonomy and were not independently re-derived here.
